abstract: "Lean 4.34.1 proofs of Fefferman's alternatives C and D of the Clay Navier-Stokes problem and of the disjunction A or B or C or D, with bridges to the authors' formulation. Contributions: OpenAI (upstream mathematics and Lean formalization, NavierStokesAndEuler, Apache-2.0); Tim Jacobs, KTS Global (the port of that library to Lean 4.34.1 and Mathlib d13f23b7, attribution operator-supplied; the statement and bridge layer, R3 per-alternative packaging and verification tooling). Not independently reviewed or reproduced; not a proof of A or B."
